From ae8d58e1c86090f50d293f04a3c86540c6ab5639 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Igor Matuszewski <xanewok@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 19:18:27 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 05/18] llama : sample from per-device top-k candidates when
 logits are vocab-split

Under SPLIT_MODE_TENSOR, output.weight and thus the logits are split by
vocab. If every backend chain starts with top-k, build_sampling takes the
top k of each device's slice, gathers the n_devices*k (logit, vocab id)
pairs to every device with ggml_backend_meta_gather and runs the chains on
those candidates. The union of the per-slice top-k contains the global
top-k, so a chain samples as it would from the full row (up to ties at the
k-th logit).

Vocab ids come from a small F32 tensor "output_vocab_ids" per context,
which the split-state callback splits exactly like output.weight. With
several sequences, the candidates of all output rows are gathered at once
and k is the largest leading top-k over the chains.

Not used yet: set_sampler still refuses backend samplers under tensor split.
